## Language, Direction & Typography

The entire website must be Persian (Farsi).

* Set `<html lang="fa" dir="rtl">` in the root layout.
* Use the **Vazirmatn** font via `next/font` (weights 400, 500, 700), wired to
  `--font-sans` in the `@theme` block.
* Render all numbers (prices, phone numbers) in Persian digits using
  `toLocaleString('fa-IR')`.

### RTL correctness — important

Use Tailwind **logical properties** throughout so the layout flips correctly:

* Use `ps-*` / `pe-*` (padding start/end), `ms-*` / `me-*` (margin start/end),
  `start-*` / `end-*`, and `text-start` / `text-end`.
* Do NOT use `pl-*`, `pr-*`, `ml-*`, `mr-*`, `left-*`, `right-*`, `text-left` or
  `text-right` — these do not flip in RTL and will produce a mirrored, broken
  layout.

The visual hierarchy should feel natural for Persian users.

